package "main"

// Regression: an indexed STORE into a NAMED managed-slice (`type Buf @[]int`).
// The slice-set arm of genAssign (pkg/binate/ir/gen_control.bn) must read the
// element type from the PEELED slice type, not the raw `collection.Typ`: a named
// slice is TYP_NAMED with a nil `.Elem` (the body hangs off `.Underlying`), so the
// un-peeled read yields a nil element type and EmitSliceSet builds a GEP with a
// nil result element.  The native backend's ElemSizeOf then returns 0, its
// emitGetElemPtr early-returns without assigning the GEP's result register, and
// the store writes through an uninitialized address slot -> SIGSEGV (empty stdout).
// LLVM masks it by defaulting a nil-element GEP to i64 (latent wrong-stride for a
// non-8-byte named element).  Isolated from 918, which also covers the struct
// field copy/dtor path.

type Buf @[]int

func main() {
	var b Buf = make_slice(int, 2)
	b[0] = 7
	println(b[0]) // 7
}
